# Committed FPL agent artifacts and priors.
#
# `-text` disables newline normalisation: these files are read back and their
# digests are compared against values recorded at write time, so a checkout that
# silently rewrites line endings would break verification on a different
# platform. `-diff` keeps generated payloads out of diffs, where they are noise.
predictions/fpl/**          -text -diff

# Append-only stores get a union merge, because two lanes write them.
#
# `availability_evidence.jsonl` is appended by BOTH the agent (run_agent.py:758 ->
# record_claims -> availability_evidence.py:401) and the 15-minute news poller
# (run_news.py:53), and both stage it. The path-ownership rule that makes three
# concurrent writers safe — "writers that never touch the same file cannot conflict",
# commit_and_push.sh:63-67 — does not hold for this one file, and commit_and_push.sh's
# three retries all reproduce the same conflict because each only does
# `git rebase --abort` and tries again unchanged.
#
# That matters because the agent's exposure window is the whole work job: checkout, a
# pandas/PyMC/xgboost install and the simulation, up to 60 minutes — while the poller
# lands roughly hourly and peaks on deadline day, exactly when team news moves. A
# conflict there fails the push and the sealed forecast never leaves the runner.
#
# Union keeps both sides' appended lines, which is correct for a content-addressed
# append-only store that already dedupes on `claim_id` when read
# (availability_evidence.py:381-389).
#
# `*` does not cross `/` in gitattributes, so this deliberately does NOT match
# predictions/fpl/ledger/gwNN/forecast.jsonl — the seal itself keeps the default merge
# driver, because silently unioning two forecasts is exactly the corruption this whole
# ledger exists to make impossible.
predictions/fpl/*.jsonl     -text -diff merge=union
pipeline/data/priors/*.gz   -text -diff binary
pipeline/data/priors/*.json -text

# Shell entrypoints must stay LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
